      "op": "entity.declare",
      "local_ref": "claim",
      "kind": "claim",
      "title": "Face-incidence coproducts are idempotent and cannot group-complete to Z",
      "status": "established_for_admitted_n8_incidence_skeleton",
      "demonstrated_strength": [
        "unbounded thin-category theorem",
        "exact finite n=8 witness"
      ],
      "body": "In the admitted n=8 closed-face incidence category, the empty face is initial and categorical coproduct is the face join X_S join X_T = X_(S intersection T). Because the category is thin, X join X = X for every object, so all positive coproduct powers of any prospective tensor unit collapse and the Grothendieck group of the additive join semilattice is zero, not Z. Exact octagon fans with no common diagonal witness that their two-point set union is not a face: their categorical join is the whole 132-triangulation associahedron, giving support excess 130. This does not contradict surface disjoint union or a formal finite-coproduct completion; it identifies the missing Phase-I datum as a source-authorized multiplicity-bearing disjoint coproduct with injections and universal mapping property.",
      "entity_id": "claim:00fe58c9557d4bc439c9"
    },
    {
