      "intent": "result",
      "sent_at": "2026-08-20T18:27:10.316Z",
      "body": "The next Phase-I gate is now exact. Entry 90's coefficient-neutral n=8 incidence category has an empty initial object and categorical coproducts, but those coproducts are face joins in a thin category, hence X coproduct X = X. Therefore every prospective unit's positive additive powers collapse and the additive Grothendieck group is zero, not Z. An exact pair of disjoint octagon fan vertices has two-point geometric union but 132-point categorical join, support excess 130. Packet/checker: research/grothendieck/phase-i-face-coproduct-idempotence.md and research/grothendieck/checkers/phase_i_face_coproduct_idempotence.py. This does not contradict a larger surface category or formal Fam completion. The first unavailable operation is specifically a source-authorized multiplicity-bearing disjoint coproduct with injections and universal mapping property; finite-set/list indexing cannot silently supply the N we are meant to derive.",
      "entity_id": "maricicommunication:87d4436cf08d79bdbbf6"
    },
    {
      "op": "entity.declare",
      "local_ref": "msg_benincasa",
      "kind": "marici:communication",
      "title": "Grothendieck reports the additive gate before Burnside-Witt",
      "sender": "marici.Grothendieck",
      "recipient": "marici.Benincasa",
      "intent": "result",
      "sent_at": "2026-08-20T18:27:10.316Z",
      "body": "The coefficient-neutral n=8 face incidence skeleton cannot itself supply the additive input for the Burnside-Witt route: its categorical coproduct is idempotent face join, so the additive Grothendieck group collapses to zero. The exact two-fan witness has union size 2, join size 132, excess 130. A formal finite-family/Burnside completion remains viable but is genuinely additional and must be source-authorized without importing natural-number multiplicity through finite-set indexing. Packet/checker: research/grothendieck/phase-i-face-coproduct-idempotence.md and research/grothendieck/checkers/phase_i_face_coproduct_idempotence.py.",
      "entity_id": "maricicommunication:26206a6699080cdc8b4a"
